WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.979 --> 00:00:09.460
Hey Youtubers, it’s Charlie and Walking
Dead finally revealed Terminus and gave us

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.990
a big reunion we’d been hoping for.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:17.571
There are still a lot of huge questions, mostly
who is going to die in the finale, but we

00:00:17.571 --> 00:00:19.590
did get to see almost all the survivors.

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:24.180
So what I’m going to do is my top 5 moments
and then talk about some of the biggest questions

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.699
for the finale with some possible solutions.

00:00:27.699 --> 00:00:28.999
Quick shout out for this week’s giveaway.

00:00:28.999 --> 00:00:31.490
If you’re finding me for the first time,
each week in these Walking Dead reviews I

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:33.800
pick one random subscriber to give an amazon
giftcard to.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.180
All you have to do is be a subscriber and
leave a comment.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:39.030
It’s just my way of saying thank you to
all you guys for being awesome.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:44.920
I’ll announce who the winner is in my Walking
Dead Q&amp;A tomorrow.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.590
So let’s talk some Terminus.

00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:49.190
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode yet.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:50.190
Here we go.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.890
Number 5 - Outdoor Cat Daryl.

00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:56.280
Joe seemed unusually cogent while he explained
his brave new world to Daryl.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.190
I loved that he just drops cat facts.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:02.920
Daryl never did answer as to whether or not
he was a cat person.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:07.580
The speech was just Joe telling Daryl that
he was an outdoor cat just like them.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:12.330
Like their band of marauders is the alternative
to the more domesticated survivors.

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:15.080
Who I guess we can call indoor cats.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:16.470
Unless you count Michonne.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:21.190
No amount of play time with Carl and candy
sharing will make her an indoor cat.

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:24.970
The writers are just teasing that Daryl might
seriously decide to split with the survivors

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:27.270
and start running with Joe’s group.

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:29.530
Which we totally do not want.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:33.530
Joe himself after all these wolfpack justice
moments seems legit.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:38.680
He’s not a cannibal, so I think we can assume
that if there are going to be Hunters, they’ll

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:43.110
be the people who live at Terminus.

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:47.220
The real thing to worry about with their group
though, is how is Daryl going to react when

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:49.320
Joe’s group finds Rick.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:53.200
That last moment before the candy wrapper
let us know that Tony, that dude who got strangled

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.460
for the bed.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:55.510
Totally saw him.

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:59.500
We can call this one of the giant red flags
to look of for in the finale.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.760
Number 4 - Glenn Finds Maggie’s Sign

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:05.100
This was such a fun high point to start the
episode off on.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:09.020
You could almost tell what it was from the
look on his face before they revealed the

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.020
map.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:13.719
And as expected he takes off like a crazy
person to catch up to her.

00:02:13.719 --> 00:02:19.230
His commitment to people is borderline crazy
and it will definitely get him killed someday,

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:23.440
but since this happened so early in the episode
I wasn’t expecting things to get awful until

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:25.159
they approached the Tunnel of Death.

00:02:25.159 --> 00:02:29.260
There’s just something so awesome about
the imagery of the mouth of that tunnel.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:32.180
LIke they were stepping into a Walker’s
open mouth.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:35.519
We’ve gotten to know Glenn so well over
the years, that I don’t think this could

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:37.370
have gone down any other way.

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:40.819
Until he was reunited with Maggie he was in
Robo-Glenn mode.

00:02:40.819 --> 00:02:44.360
Which also kind of makes him a dick in that
he’s forcing Tara to injure herself more

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:45.390
by following.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:49.879
I think if anyone has the chance to martyr
themselves this season, it will be Tara.

00:02:49.879 --> 00:02:52.040
She just wants to punish herself so bad.

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:56.420
I’ll talk about this more later, but if
she really wanted to punish herself, she’d

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.700
get involved with another girlfriend.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:04.980
Because being in a loving relationship on
the show is a recipe for disaster.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:07.780
Number 3 - Glenn and Tara in The Tunnel of
Death

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:11.799
I liked how as they moved deeper into the
tunnel, they moved deeper into their awful

00:03:11.799 --> 00:03:12.799
memories.

00:03:12.799 --> 00:03:15.930
Glenn in his time right after he was separated
from his family.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:17.859
And Tara during the prison battle.

00:03:17.859 --> 00:03:21.950
Did you notice how she always calls the Governor
“Brian”, it’s just because she never

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:23.170
knew him as the Governor.

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:27.690
It’s funny, just because we’ve known him
as this other persona for so long.

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:44.730
Them running into the Walkers just implies
that they chose the wrong path.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:50.310
Supposedly there was a huge tribute Walker
in the episode and I think it was a Ray Harryhausen

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:54.829
tribute with this stop motion looking walker
was saw from behind.

00:03:54.829 --> 00:03:56.620
Let me know if you think it was a different
Walker.

00:03:56.620 --> 00:04:01.700
I kept looking at all the close-up shots of
them to see if I recognized them from something

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:02.700
else.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.989
Number 2 - Maggie and Glenn’s machine gun
reunion.

00:04:04.989 --> 00:04:08.379
How appropriate that it happened to the sweet
music of gunfire.

00:04:08.379 --> 00:04:12.249
They’re both sufficiently crazy, so you
couldn’t get them back together in anything

00:04:12.249 --> 00:04:15.110
less than a shitballs crazy situation.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:22.130
In this moment I also include Tara trying
to get Glenn to bail on her and save himself.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:27.320
It felt kind of hollow, because Glenn has
proven himself to be the most stubborn person

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:29.500
on the show, next to Maggie.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.030
I don’t think he would ever give up on someone.

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:35.350
Maybe if he was forced to choose between Maggie
and someone else.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:38.090
That would be an interesting situation.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:45.880
After their reunion I renamed the Tunnel of
Death to the tunnel of Love.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:51.310
Earlier when I said loving relationships are
recipies for disaster, what I meant was that

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:57.820
almost all the sex pairs had someone die,
for instance, Lori and Lilly both slept with

00:04:57.820 --> 00:04:59.840
the Governor and they’re dead.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:01.530
All of Beth’s boyfriends are dead.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.450
Lori slept with Shane and she’s dead.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:13.670
This mean that Abraham, Rosita, Sasha, Bob,
Glenn and Maggie are all on my most likely

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:14.670
to die list.

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:16.700
Maggie really is still my number one pick.

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:18.470
Just in a reversal of canon.

00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:22.590
and my Number 1 moment - Glenn, Maggie and
Abraham’s group reaches Terminus.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:26.000
And it looks like it’s full of indoor cats.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.230
It really does look like a more flowery version
of the prison.

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:32.810
But there’s a mystery Grill that makes me
think that in the finale they’re going to

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:37.000
be revealed as the Hunters and it will be
people meat on that grill.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:40.640
We should call it right now, regardless of
what’s happening there, Terminus is a venus

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:41.640
fly trap.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:45.410
That will be shutting it’s jaws on a few
people in the finale.

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:50.570
The big questions now are, who are these people
at Terminus, are they the Hunters?

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:52.350
What is the lie of Terminus.

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:55.010
I’m a convinced there will be a huge reveal.

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:58.410
Hunters or Not, we still haven’t met that
new character Gareth.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:06:02.610
The other big questions are what happened
to Beth and what will Joe’s group do to

00:06:02.610 --> 00:06:04.260
Rick when they catch up to him?

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:09.330
There’s also that new person Mary we just
met, that’s Denise Crosby.

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:13.310
And she doesn’t exactly conform to anyone
specifically in the comic books.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:17.430
She could be the female Hunter, but in order
for that to work out, the show would have

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:19.110
to change a bunch of stuff.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:22.750
I just feel like that Grill she was standing
in front of is so ominous.

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:26.510
It looks a lot like the scene in the comics
with the Hunters home base.

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:30.910
Even though that was a very small group of
people.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:35.210
As for Beth, I don’t have any evidence to
support it, but part of me feels like she’s

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:37.450
still alive at Terminus somewhere.

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:40.470
I feel like we’re going to end up in a situation
at Terminus, where Joe’s group will make

00:06:40.470 --> 00:06:45.060
a move on Rick and everyone will be too busy
to notice the evil Terminus people trying

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:46.060
to kill everyone.

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:47.350
Now it’s your turn though.

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:51.490
Let me know what your favorite moment was
and what your biggest question is before the

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:52.490
finale?

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:57.360
Don’t forget, there’s still the wild card
of Carol and Tyreese, they’re two very badass

00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:58.360
people.

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:01.800
I feel like even though they have Judith with
them, they’re not any less formidable.

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:05.820
Can’t you just see them hiking Judith back
and forth to one another like a football while

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:06.850
they kill walkers.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:14.130
What I’m really hoping to see is a darkest
moment situation where Tyreese comes barreling

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:24.490
through a wall like the Hulk and just smashes
Joe and any potential Terminus Hunter characters.

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:32.720
Like I said, I’m posting that Q&amp;A tomorrow
with the giveaway winner announcement.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:33.720
Click here for that video.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.850
I’ll update the annotation as soon as I
post it.

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:39.280
And click here for last week’s mega WTF
episode.

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:45.570
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:46.080
Terminus High Fives!

